152-
153-**Your local run gets claimed and failed by a prod worker.** A prod worker pod polling the same database will claim your pending runs and fail them out from under local dev. The fix is to stop sharing the database: point `DATABASE_URL` at a local or embedded Postgres (see "Isolating a benchmark/scratch server" above). Scaling the prod worker deployment down is a production change, not a dev step — it stops real users' runs, so it requires the deployment owner's explicit approval, a coordinated maintenance window, and a restore plan; never run an ad hoc `kubectl scale` mid-debug.
