      "title": "[P1] Do not pair cached identity with fresh output",
      "body": "When ChatGPT reuses an iframe and updates `toolOutput` while the previous card remains in `widgetState`, `data` comes from the live output but this still returns the old widget `resultIdentity`. The provider then records and persists that identity for the current card, so delayed metadata for the old token can restore old view state/tool information and bind the old snapshot to a new host ID. Only expose the widget identity when data came from that same widget snapshot, or discard it whenever `hasToolOutput` is true.",
